  "id": "area-under-the-curve",
  "term": "area under the curve",
  "definition": "Area under the curve (AUC) is a summary number from a receiver operating characteristic curve that shows how well a test can distinguish between positive and negative cases. It can be understood as the chance that a randomly chosen positive case will have a higher test result than a randomly chosen negative case.",
